  "content": {
    "protected": false,
    "rendered": "<div class=\"xyz-content\"><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"shell pt-6\"> <ol class=\"m-0 flex list-none flex-wrap items-center gap-2 p-0 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-soft\"> <li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\">  <a href=\"/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Home </a> </li><li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <a href=\"/tax-tips/\" class=\"no-underline hover:underline\"> Resources </a> </li><li class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"> <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"text-rule\"> / </span> <span aria-current=\"page\">The <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> standard deduction: what it is and who it helps</span> </li> </ol> </nav> <article class=\"shell pt-6\"> <header class=\"max-w-3xl\"> <p class=\"band-eyebrow\">Resources</p> <h1 class=\"text-3xl sm:text-4xl\">The <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> standard deduction: what it is and who it helps</h1> <p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.125rem] text-ink\">From 1 July 2026, ITAA 1997 s 25-130 lets you claim a <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> standard deduction for work-related expenses with no receipts at all. You get whichever is higher — the <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> or your itemised claim — applied automatically.</p> <p class=\"mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[0.75rem] tabular-nums text-ink-soft\"> <span>Updated 21 August 2026</span> <span>Current for 2026-27</span> </p> </header> <div class=\"prose-statement mt-10\">  <p>This is the largest change to individual deductions in years, and it applies to the year you are earning in right now — not the one you are lodging.</p> <h2 id=\"what-actually-changed\">What actually changed</h2> <p>Before 1 July 2026, every dollar of work-related expenses you claimed had to be money you had actually spent, on something connected to earning your income, with a record to show for it. The <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$300</span> substantiation threshold softened the record-keeping, but you still needed to have spent the money.</p> <p>From 1 July 2026, ITAA 1997 s 25-130 gives you a floor. You can claim</p> <p><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span> of work-related expenses without receipts and without having spent anything. It is not a rebate and not a payment — it is a deduction, so what it is worth to you depends on your marginal rate.</p> <h2 id=\"what-it-is-worth\">What it is worth</h2> <p>A deduction reduces the income you are taxed on, so its value is your marginal rate plus the Medicare levy:</p> <table><thead><tr><th>Your taxable income</th><th>Marginal rate</th><th>The <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> is worth</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$30,000</span></td><td>15%</td><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$170</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$60,000</span></td><td>30%</td><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$320</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$100,000</span></td><td>30%</td><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$320</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$150,000</span></td><td>37%</td><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$390</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$200,000</span></td><td>45%</td><td><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$470</span></td></tr></tbody></table> <p>For most people that is between <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-return text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$170</span> and</p> <p><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-return text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$470</span>. It arrives as a larger refund rather than a separate payment.</p> <h2 id=\"the-part-people-get-wrong\">The part people get wrong</h2> <p><strong>It replaces your itemised claim, it does not add to it.</strong> You get the higher of the two, not both. If your real work-related expenses come to</p> <p><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,400</span>, you claim <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,400</span> and the standard deduction is irrelevant to you. If they come to <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$400</span>, you claim <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span>.</p> <p><strong>It only covers work-related expenses.</strong> The categories at D1 to D5 on the return: car, travel, uniforms, self-education and other work expenses. It does not displace anything outside those. Investment property deductions, interest and dividend deductions, personal super contributions, donations and the cost of managing your tax affairs are all claimed on top, in full.</p> <p>So someone with <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$200</span> of work expenses, a</p> <p><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$500</span> donation and <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$99</span> paid to last year’s accountant claims <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span> plus <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$599</span>, not <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span> flat.</p> <h2 id=\"who-is-better-off-and-who-should-still-keep-receipts\">Who is better off, and who should still keep receipts</h2> <p>Better off: anyone whose genuine work-related expenses come to less than</p> <p><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span>. That is a large share of office workers, most casual and part-time employees, and almost every student.</p> <p>No difference: anyone already claiming more than <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span>. Nurses with registration and uniform costs, tradies with tools, teachers buying classroom materials, and anyone claiming a meaningful work-from-home amount are usually well past the floor already — a full year of home-office hours alone often exceeds it.</p> <p>The practical advice has not changed for that second group: keep the records. The standard deduction is a floor, not a ceiling, and giving up</p> <p><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$2,000</span> of real deductions to avoid keeping receipts costs you money.</p> <h2 id=\"when-it-applies\">When it applies</h2> <p>The provision applies from the 2026-27 income year, which began on 1 July 2026. That means:</p> <ul> <li>The return you are lodging <strong>now</strong>, for the year ended 30 June 2026, does not get it. That year is 2025-26 and the old rules apply.</li> <li>The return you lodge from July 2027 does.</li> </ul> <p>Switch the financial year selector in the calculator below between 2025-26 and 2026-27 to see the difference on your own income — it moves alongside the second marginal rate falling from 16% to 15%, so the two changes compound.</p> <h2 id=\"does-it-change-whether-you-need-an-accountant\">Does it change whether you need an accountant?</h2> <p>For a genuinely simple return — one job, no investments, no side income, few expenses — it makes self-lodging slightly simpler, and we would rather tell you that than pretend otherwise.</p> <p>Where it changes nothing is the case that was always worth advice: multiple income sources, an investment property, capital gains, a business, or a year where something unusual happened. Those returns are not decided by the work-related expenses line, and a <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums tracking-tight text-ink text-[0.8125rem] font-medium\">$1,000</span> floor does not touch them.</p>  </div> </article> <section class=\"shell mt-16\"> <h2 class=\"text-xl\">Put a number on it</h2> <p class=\"mt-2 max-w-2xl text-[0.9375rem]\"> Your tax, Medicare levy, study loan repayment and take-home pay for any income, in any of the last three financial years. Free, and it works without an email address. </p> <div class=\"mt-6\"> <div id=\"xyz-island-0\" data-xyz-island=\"TaxCalculator\" data-xyz-props=\"{}\"><div class=\"grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_23rem] lg:gap-12\"><div class=\"min-w-0\"><div class=\"rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_2l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Your income before tax</label><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$1,635<!-- -->/week</span></div><div class=\"mt-2\"><div class=\"relative\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 font-mono text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$</span><input id=\"_r1R_2l_\" type=\"text\" inputMode=\"decimal\" autoComplete=\"off\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)] pl-7 text-right\" placeholder=\"0\" value=\"85,000\"/></div></div><p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Salary, wages or total business income for the year.</p></div><div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_4l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Financial year</label></div><div class=\"mt-2\"><select id=\"_r1R_4l_\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)]\"><option value=\"2024-25\">2024–25</option><option value=\"2025-26\">2025–26</option><option value=\"2026-27\" selected=\"\">2026–27 (current)</option></select></div><p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Includes the <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> standard deduction, applied automatically.</p></div><div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_6l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Work-related deductions</label></div><div class=\"mt-2\"><div class=\"relative\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 font-mono text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$</span><input id=\"_r1R_6l_\" type=\"text\" inputMode=\"decimal\" autoComplete=\"off\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)] pl-7 text-right\" placeholder=\"0\" value=\"\"/></div></div><p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Leave blank to take the <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$1,000</span> standard deduction. Enter more only if you can beat it.</p></div><div class=\"py-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] last:border-b-0\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3\"><label for=\"_r1R_8l_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Residency for tax purposes</label></div><div class=\"mt-2\"><select id=\"_r1R_8l_\" class=\"w-full rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white px-3 py-2.5 text-[var(--color-ink)] focus:border-[var(--color-signal)]\"><option value=\"resident\" selected=\"\">Australian resident</option><option value=\"foreign\">Foreign resident</option><option value=\"working-holiday\">Working holiday maker</option></select></div><p class=\"mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Foreign residents pay tax from the first dollar and no Medicare levy.</p></div><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] py-4 last:border-b-0\"><div class=\"max-w-sm\"><label for=\"_r1R_al_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">I have a HECS-HELP or study loan</label><p class=\"mt-1 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Repayments start at <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$69,528</span> and are marginal — only the income above the threshold counts.</p></div><input id=\"_r1R_al_\" type=\"checkbox\" class=\"mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 accent-[var(--color-signal)]\"/></div><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] py-4 last:border-b-0\"><div class=\"max-w-sm\"><label for=\"_r1R_cl_\" class=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">I have private hospital cover</label><p class=\"mt-1 mb-0 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Without it, high earners pay the Medicare levy surcharge on top of the levy.</p></div><input id=\"_r1R_cl_\" type=\"checkbox\" class=\"mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 accent-[var(--color-signal)]\" checked=\"\"/></div><fieldset class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] py-4 last:border-b-0 m-0 p-0\"><legend class=\"mb-2 p-0 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Show my numbers</legend><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-1 rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white p-1\"><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"flex-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-[2px] px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.8125rem] transition-colors text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\">Weekly</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"flex-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-[2px] px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.8125rem] transition-colors text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\">Fortnightly</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"flex-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-[2px] px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.8125rem] transition-colors text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\">Monthly</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"flex-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-[2px] px-3 py-1.5 text-[0.8125rem] transition-colors bg-[var(--color-ink)] font-semibold text-[var(--color-paper)]\">Annually</button></div></fieldset></div><div class=\"mt-4\"><div class=\"rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white p-5\"><h2 class=\"m-0 font-display text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\">How the scale applies to you</h2><p class=\"mt-1 mb-4 text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">Your top dollar is taxed at<!-- --> <strong class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink)]\">30%</strong>, but across the whole income you pay<!-- --> <strong class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink)]\">20.71%</strong>. Earning a dollar more never leaves you worse off.</p><div><div class=\"flex h-3 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-[2px] bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Income of $84,000 split across the 2026-27 tax brackets\"><div style=\"width:21.666666666666668%;background:#C9D3D0\" class=\"h-full\"></div><div style=\"width:31.9047619047619%;background:#9FB1AE\" class=\"h-full\"></div><div style=\"width:46.42857142857143%;background:#6E8481\" class=\"h-full\"></div></div><table class=\"mt-4 text-[0.8125rem]\"><caption class=\"sr-only\">Tax by bracket for <!-- -->2026-27</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Bracket</th><th scope=\"col\">Rate</th><th scope=\"col\">Your income</th><th scope=\"col\">Tax</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"\"><th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$0<!-- -->–$18,200</th><td class=\"font-mono\">0%</td><td class=\"font-mono\">$18,200</td><td class=\"font-mono font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">$0</td></tr><tr class=\"\"><th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$18,201<!-- -->–$45,000</th><td class=\"font-mono\">15%</td><td class=\"font-mono\">$26,800</td><td class=\"font-mono font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">$4,020</td></tr><tr class=\"\"><th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$45,001<!-- -->–$135,000</th><td class=\"font-mono\">30%</td><td class=\"font-mono\">$39,000</td><td class=\"font-mono font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">$11,700</td></tr><tr class=\"text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$135,001<!-- -->–$190,000</th><td class=\"font-mono\">37%</td><td class=\"font-mono\">$0</td><td class=\"font-mono font-medium \">$0</td></tr><tr class=\"text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><th scope=\"row\" class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] font-normal normal-case tracking-normal\">$190,001<!-- -->+</th><td class=\"font-mono\">45%</td><td class=\"font-mono\">$0</td><td class=\"font-mono font-medium \">$0</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div><div class=\"min-w-0 lg:sticky lg:top-6 lg:self-start\"><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-[4px] border border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-white\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-paper)]\">Take-home pay</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.6875rem] tabular-nums text-[var(--color-paper)]/70\">2026–27 · Annually</span></div><div class=\"tally-print\"><div data-tally-line=\"gross\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Gross income</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$85,000</span></span></div></div><div data-tally-line=\"deductions\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Less deductions</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">−</span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$1,000</span></span></div></div><div data-tally-line=\"taxable\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Taxable income</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums font-semibold\" aria-hidden=\"true\">$84,000</span></span></div></div><div data-tally-line=\"income-tax\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Income tax</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$15,720</span></span></div></div><div data-tally-line=\"medicare\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] \"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Medicare levy</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums \" aria-hidden=\"true\">$1,680</span></span></div></div><div data-tally-line=\"total-tax\" class=\"border-b border-[var(--color-rule)] bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)]\"><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-2.5\"><button type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-left text-[0.8125rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"inline-block text-[0.625rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)] transition-transform \">▶</span>Total tax</button><span class=\"shrink-0 text-[0.9375rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\"></span><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums font-semibold\" aria-hidden=\"true\">$17,400</span></span></div></div></div><div data-tally-line=\"take-home\" class=\"px-4 py-5\"><div class=\"flex items-end justify-between gap-4\"><div><p class=\"m-0 text-[0.8125rem] font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\">Take-home pay</p><p class=\"m-0 mt-0.5 max-w-[22rem] text-[0.6875rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">What lands in your account across the year, before salary sacrifice.</p></div><div class=\"flex h-11 shrink-0 items-center\"><span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]\" aria-hidden=\"true\">$67,600</span></div></div><p class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"polite\">Take-home pay<!-- -->:<!-- --> <span class=\"font-mono tabular-nums\">$67,600</span></p><p class=\"m-0 mt-2 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] tabular-nums text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">$85,000 − $17,400</p><div class=\"mt-4\"><div class=\"space-y-3\"><p class=\"m-0 rounded-[3px] bg-[var(--color-paper-sunk)] px-3 py-2 text-[0.75rem] text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">What changed: on this income you keep<!-- --> <strong class=\"font-mono tabular-nums text-[var(--color-return)]\">$588</strong> <!-- -->more<!-- --> than in <!-- -->2025–26<!-- -->.</p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://brsadvisory.myassembly.com/login?step=signUp&amp;income=85000&amp;fy=2026-27\" class=\"block rounded-[4px] bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-paper)] no-underline\">Lodge with a registered agent</a><p class=\"m-0 text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]\">An estimate, not tax advice. Your assessment is determined by the ATO.<!-- --> Some 2026–27 thresholds are not yet indexed by the ATO and carry forward from the prior year.</p></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mt-3 text-center text-[0.6875rem] t